          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            embeds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithfully"} fully faithfully
            into the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Multicat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Multicat
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
            in two ways:
          %ol
            %li As the unary multicategories (i.e. in which every multimorphism has unary domain).
            %li
              Via the “discrete cocones” construction, in which we define the multimorphisms of the multicategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo ▸
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\blacktriangleright
              induced by a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo ▸
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo ;
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C_\blacktriangleright(X_1, \ldots, X_n; Y) := C(X_1, Y) \times \cdots \times C(X_n, Y)
          %p
            A multicategory is isomorphic to one induced by the discrete cocones construction exactly when it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
            relative to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
            whose algebras are categories with (strict) finite coproducts, i.e. a “virtual cocartesian category”. Thus, such a multicategory is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong cocartesian multicategory
          %p
            An older name for a cocartesian multicategory is a
            = succeed "," do
              %em sequential multicategory
          %h2#equivalence_of_definitions Equivalence of definitions
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategory"} symmetric multicategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              the following are equivalent.
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo ≅
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo ▸
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \cong C_\blacktriangleright
                  for some category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  (which then must be the category of unary morphisms in
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %li
                %p
                  Every object of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %li
                %p
                  Every object of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+magma"} unital magma
                  object, in a way that commutes with all the multimorphisms of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  is equipped with
                %ul
                  %li
                    “expansion” operations (the dual of
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contraction+rule"} contraction
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi …
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi …
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi …
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi …
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\dots, x, \dots) \to E(\dots, x,x,\dots)
                  %li
                    “strengthening” operations (the dual of
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakening+rule"} weakening
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi …
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi …
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi …
                            %mo ,
                            %mi …
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\dots, x,\dots) \to E(\dots, \dots)
                %p satisfying certain evident axioms.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  has the structure of a virtual
                  = succeed "-algebra," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  is the monad on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
                  whose algebras are cocartesian strict monoidal categories.
            %p
          %p
            The equivalence of (1)–(3) is Proposition 3.6 (3.7 in the arXiv version v1) of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Pisani14"} Pisani 14
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              In (5), the additional structure in a virtual cocartesian category beyond that of a virtual symmetric monoidal category (that is, a symmetric multicategory) consists of generalized
              = succeed "-ary" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p It is easy to check that (1) implies all the other conditions, and of course (2) implies (3).
            %p
              Now assuming (3), the free symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F E
              generated by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fox%27s+theorem"} Fox's theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F E
              is cocartesian monoidal. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              embeds fully in the underlying multicategory of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F E
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo ;
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ×
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo ;
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(x_1,\dots, x_n; y) \cong E(x_1;y) \times \cdots \times E(x_n;y)
            %p
              It therefore suffices to show that (5) implies (3). The magma structure maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi mult
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} mult_x \in E(x,x;x)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi unit
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} unit_x \in E(;x)
              are obtained by expansion and strengthening from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ;
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_x\in E(x;x)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              Write
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = \{1,\dots ,n\}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A
              has as objects finite lists of objects of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1,\dots, a_m) \to (a'_1,\dots ,a'_n)
              given by a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi m
                    %mo →
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:m\to n
              and morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{i} \to a'_{\phi(i)}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M:A
              ⇸
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T M : T A
              ⇸
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T B
              has heteromorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b_1,\dots, b_m)
              ⇸
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1,\dots, a_n)
              given by a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi m
                    %mo →
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:m\to n
              and heteromorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_i
              ⇸
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{\phi(i)}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in m
            %p
              Now a virtual
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and a profunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M : A
              ⇸
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
