          %h2#references References
          %p The discrete cocones construction was introduced in Example 2.2(2) of:
          %ul
            %li#Hermida
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Hermida"}> Claudio Hermida
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representable multicategories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://wslc.math.ist.utl.pt/s84.www/cs/claudio/articles/rep-mult.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and studied extensively in the following papers, where the terminology
            %strong sequential multicategory
            is introduced:
          %ul
            %li#Pisani13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Pisani"}> Claudio Pisani
                ,
                %em Some remarks on multicategories and additive categories,
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3033"} arXiv:1304.3033
                (2013).
            %li#Pisani14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Pisani"}> Claudio Pisani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sequential multicategories
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.0253"} arXiv:1402.0253
          %p
            It is further studied, under the name
            %strong cocartesian multicategory
            in:
          %ul
            %li#Pisani25
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Pisani"}> Claudio Pisani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Unbiased multicategory theory
              %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/44/28/44-28abs.html"} web
          %p
            The discrete cocones construction is also discussed in Example 2.1.6 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Operads%2C+Higher+Categories"} Higher Operads, Higher Categories
          %p
            An analogue of sequential multicategories for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C+1%29-categories"} (infinity, 1)-categories
            is contained in §2.4.3 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p The sequential multicategory structure was rediscovered in the one-object setting as the “T construction” of:
          %ul
            %li
              Samuele Giraudo,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Combinatorial operads from monoids
          %p
            A generalisation of the concept to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalised+multicategories"} generalised multicategories
            is given in:
          %ul
            %li
              Alex Cebrian,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Plethysms and operads
          %p References for generalized multicategories:
          %ul
            %li#CruttwellShulman10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geoff+Cruttwell"} Geoff Cruttwell
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em A unified framework for generalized multicategories
              %strong 24
              21 (2010) 580-655 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0907.2460"}> arxiv/0907.2460
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/24/21/24-21abs.html"} TAC:24-21
